WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.989 --> 00:00:06.160
As well as this video about Season 6 Episode
1, we’ve got a new video out now about the

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:09.690
final episode of The Expanse, Season 6 Episode
6.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:12.850
You can watch it now at the link below.

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:16.150
The final season of The Expanse has begun.

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:19.040
And Episode 1 is called Strange Dogs.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:24.330
Cause Season 6 is mostly adapted from the
sixth Expanse book, Babylon’s Ashes.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:29.340
But the season also adapts one of the Expanse
novellas, Strange Dogs.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:33.410
So it begins with this girl Cara on the planet
Laconia.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:40.610
Remember, last season, a bunch of rogue Martians
led by Admiral Duarte went to Laconia.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:45.070
Cara is the daughter of some scientists who
came here years earlier.

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:48.620
Cara grew up here, so Laconia is her home.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:54.760
She loves exploring, and frolicking with the
wildlife, like an extra-terrestrial Snow White.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:59.510
She sees a strange dog lookin thing she’s
never seen before.

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:02.430
And she gives food to an alien bird.

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:07.700
In the book, she describes how she read a
story about a lady on Earth who feeds bread

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:11.310
to birds, so figured she could do the same
here.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:13.689
But this isn’t Earth.

00:01:13.689 --> 00:01:20.600
Human food isn’t compatible with alien biology
– so her food hurts the bird, to Cara’s

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:21.619
horror.

00:01:21.619 --> 00:01:28.679
So Cara likes Laconia, but there’s a clash
between humanity and this alien world.

00:01:28.679 --> 00:01:33.819
Strange Dogs is about the unexpected results
of humans and aliens interacting.

00:01:33.819 --> 00:01:40.499
It’s also an immigration story, about a
kid growing up in a new place, reconciling

00:01:40.499 --> 00:01:45.539
her family’s past with her future in her
new home.

00:01:45.539 --> 00:01:50.960
We see alien structures on Laconia, just like
the ones on Ilus in Season 4.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:55.259
And we see this mysterious thing in orbit,
above the planet.

00:01:55.259 --> 00:02:01.509
We know the scientist Cortázar is studying
this thing, trying to control it, and he has

00:02:01.509 --> 00:02:04.060
a protomolecule sample.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:09.140
On the thing in orbit, we see the blue glow
of protomolecule.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:14.750
In the past, messing with the protomolecule
and alien tech has been.. disastrous.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:17.560
On Ilus, it almost blew up a whole planet.

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:21.560
In the Ring space it changed physics and killed
thousands.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:27.460
On Eros, it consumed an entire moon and all
the humans on it.

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:32.640
But Cortázar and Duarte are determined to
harness this alien power.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:36.130
What could possibly go wrong?

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:42.770
Marco Inaros, extremist leader of the Belter
Free Navy, continues to hit Earth with rocks,

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:45.850
causing apocalyptic destruction.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:52.040
Millions are dead, the environment is devastated,
the home of humanity is broken.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:57.480
In the book, we get a chapter with Anna, and
her wife and child on Earth, struggling to

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:01.750
survive under a sky dark with ash.

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:06.270
Many Belters celebrate Marco’s attack and
join his Free Navy.

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:11.570
They see it as justice that Earth is suffering,
because for a hundred years Belters have suffered

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:13.940
under Earth’s oppression.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:19.910
This Belter activist guy is the same one we
saw on Ceres back in Season 1 Episode 1.

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:24.140
He protested against Earthers taking the water
and air from Belters.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:31.430
He said in Season 1 that when a hail of stones
hits Earth, maybe then Earthers will understand

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:33.480
the suffering of the Belt.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:39.040
Now, it’s the Earthers who don’t have
water and clean air, it’s Earthers who don’t

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:44.860
have a safe home – so he says now they know
what it’s like to be Belters.

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:48.500
We see that survivors of Pallas are vowing
revenge.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:53.010
Cause Pallas is a Belter station that was
attacked by Earth last season.

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:57.460
Avasarala had argued they shouldn’t attack
Pallas because that would kill civilians and

00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:00.110
turn more Belters against Earth.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:05.510
They attacked Pallas anyway, and whaddaya
know, the survivors wants revenge.

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:09.260
Killing civilians made more terrorists.

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:14.280
Earth’s ships are defending the planet,
destroying most of the incoming rocks.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:17.039
But for Avasarala, it’s not enough.

00:04:17.039 --> 00:04:22.460
Marco’s Free Navy is growing stronger, while
Earth is dying.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:27.759
The dust thrown up by the rock strikes blocks
the sun like a nuclear winter, killing plant

00:04:27.759 --> 00:04:30.630
life, starving the planet.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:34.789
Avasarala says that she never liked shooting
stars.

00:04:34.789 --> 00:04:39.849
This calls back to Season 1, when she looked
up at shooting stars and said she worries

00:04:39.849 --> 00:04:43.240
about people throwing rocks.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:44.990
She was right to worry.

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:49.509
She mentions that they’re repurposing their
“atmospheric CO2 scrubbers” to try to

00:04:49.509 --> 00:04:51.210
clean the atmosphere.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:55.860
Maybe those CO2 scrubbers were originally
used to stop climate change on Earth.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:05:00.770
Cause the backstory in The Expanse is that
global warming made the ice caps melt, and

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:06.380
sea levels rose – we see that Anchorage
is now an island, and the statue of liberty’s

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:08.130
almost got her feet wet.

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:12.479
It was the crisis of climate change that forced
the countries of Earth to unite under the

00:05:12.479 --> 00:05:15.010
United Nations for governance.

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:19.050
And it looks like they mostly succeeded in
saving the Earth’s environment..

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:20.550
until now.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:25.639
The journalist Monica demands answers and
leadership from Avasarala.

00:05:25.639 --> 00:05:30.520
She highlights how dangerous it is that Marco
now controls the Ring space.

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:35.909
The Ring space and Medina Station are the
central hub that controls access to all thirteen

00:05:35.909 --> 00:05:37.660
hundred Ring gates.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:43.650
All of the colony worlds beyond those gates,
like Ilus, are now at the mercy of Marco.

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:48.930
Marco could be doing whatever he wants to
a thousand worlds, and Earth and Mars wouldn’t

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:50.330
even know.

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:55.879
Avasarala gets away from it all and enjoys
floating in zero gravity.

00:05:55.879 --> 00:06:03.159
Usually Avasarala hates space – “I fucking
hate space” – but now she enjoys the weightlessness.

00:06:03.159 --> 00:06:09.650
Avasarala always feels weighed down by the
responsibility of governing Earth, protecting

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:14.960
the billions of people on it, carrying the
planet like Atlas.

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:20.629
She works so hard, and still everyone blames
her for everything from riots in Kinshasa

00:06:20.629 --> 00:06:23.430
to Marco’s control of distant space.

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:28.090
In the book, she fantasises about retiring
to “some alien ocean” where she won’t

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:31.039
feel “responsible for making the waves go
up and down”.

00:06:31.039 --> 00:06:32.039
She’s still grieving her dead husband Arjun,
she’s beyond exhausted.

00:06:32.039 --> 00:06:34.190
Avasarala hates her job.

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:37.220
And her sidekick Bobbie hates hers too.

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:38.289
But millions are dying.

00:06:38.289 --> 00:06:42.789
Work needs doing, so they do it.

00:06:42.789 --> 00:06:46.990
The Roci crew hunt down and destroy a Free
Navy ship.

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:52.800
This is “Day 187” of their mission, and
there’s a sense of exhaustion, and futility,

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:54.740
among the crew.

00:06:54.740 --> 00:07:00.009
Amos suggests they should be getting paid
for this, saying they’re not soldiers, questioning

00:07:00.009 --> 00:07:01.520
their purpose here.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:07.129
The crew are still grieving the death of Alex,
they’re stressed and tense with each other.

00:07:07.129 --> 00:07:10.569
How much longer can this war go on?

00:07:10.569 --> 00:07:14.629
They find a drive on a rock intended to be
launched at Earth.

00:07:14.629 --> 00:07:19.310
Holden goes to disable it, but it warms up
to fire, which could kill him.

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:24.849
Naomi tells him to run, but instead he bravely
stays and hits it til it breaks.

00:07:24.849 --> 00:07:28.400
Which is the same strategy he used on this
coffee machine.

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:32.589
So Holden almost dies, and Naomi is upset.

00:07:32.589 --> 00:07:37.779
The books talk about how stressful and painful
it is for her when Holden constantly throws

00:07:37.779 --> 00:07:44.349
himself into danger – he plays the hero
and risks his life all the time so Naomi can

00:07:44.349 --> 00:07:46.729
never feel that her partner is safe.

00:07:46.729 --> 00:07:51.309
So Holden realises that he’s “kind of
an asshole” to do that to her.

00:07:51.309 --> 00:07:55.229
He promises Naomi to be more careful for all
of them.

00:07:55.229 --> 00:07:57.680
Is that a promise he can keep?

00:07:57.680 --> 00:07:59.949
Clarissa Mao is on the Roci now.

00:07:59.949 --> 00:08:04.789
She once killed a bunch of people, and tried
to kill Holden, but Amos made friends with

00:08:04.789 --> 00:08:06.889
her and brought her on board.

00:08:06.889 --> 00:08:09.509
Amos and Clarissa work together well.

00:08:09.509 --> 00:08:14.400
She’s learned quickly to be a mechanic – she
mentions that she didn’t have much experience

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:19.569
with this stuff in her old life – she used
to spend more time planning fancy parties,

00:08:19.569 --> 00:08:22.720
as we saw in a Season 3 flashback.

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:26.969
Naomi doesn’t like Clarissa, and gets angry
at Amos for bringing her.

00:08:26.969 --> 00:08:31.120
‘Do you think you can do whatever you like
now’, she asks.

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:37.550
Amos used to be totally loyal and obedient
to Naomi, almost like he was her son – Miller

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:41.740
called him Naomi’s “200-pound, homicidal
kid”.

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:47.820
But now, Amos has grown up, and become more
independent from Naomi – and he’s got

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:51.430
his own homicidal follower now in Clarissa.

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:55.930
So Naomi is having trouble accepting this
new independent Amos.

00:08:55.930 --> 00:09:00.339
With Clarissa on board and Alex dead, the
relationships on the Roci are changing, everything’s

00:09:00.339 --> 00:09:01.339
uncertain.

00:09:01.339 --> 00:09:02.870
Even Amos is questioning his place in the
crew.

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:06.510
Can this unlikely family stay together?

00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:11.779
Holden discovers footage of the Laconian ship
the Barkeith being eaten by the mysterious

00:09:11.779 --> 00:09:14.029
alien entities in the Ring.

00:09:14.029 --> 00:09:18.240
Remember, we saw its destruction at the end
of last season.

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:23.279
Holden says this reminds him of this artefact
on Ilus, which was a weapon used by the entities

00:09:23.279 --> 00:09:27.699
to destroy the Builders who made the Ring
billions of years ago.

00:09:27.699 --> 00:09:33.790
So on top of their family fracturing, Earth
dying, Laconians having protomolecule, and

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:40.110
Naomi’s evil ex conquering space, they’ve
also got interdimensional genocidal aliens

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:41.740
to worry about.

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:46.490
Naomi figures out that Marco’s rocks are
being guided by a spotter ship called the

00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:47.870
Azure Dragon.

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:52.620
If they can destroy it, they could reduce
the threat to Earth, and free up Earth’s

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:54.410
ships to go after Marco.

00:09:54.410 --> 00:10:00.019
This could be the victory Earth desperately
needs against the Free Navy Belters.

00:10:00.019 --> 00:10:02.990
But Naomi has mixed feelings.

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:06.519
She’s a Belter, these are her people they’re
fighting against.

00:10:06.519 --> 00:10:09.810
Her son Filip is with the Free Navy.

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:14.050
Can she go to war against her own child?

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:19.250
Marco’s Free Navy takes over Ceres, the
biggest port in the Belt.

00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:23.940
Back in Season 1 Episode 1, we learned that
Ceres is the gateway for “immense wealth

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:29.290
and resources” – but Ceres was controlled
by Earth, who exploited and oppressed the

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:31.019
Belters who lived there.

00:10:31.019 --> 00:10:35.610
So OPA leader Anderson Dawes worked to make
Ceres politically independent – to make

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:39.500
it a home for Belters, run by Belters.

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:40.560
And he succeeded.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:45.600
By Season 2, Dawes was running Ceres as an
OPA Belter station.

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:51.110
Through long, careful management the great
negotiator outlasted his status as a rebel

00:10:51.110 --> 00:10:54.430
and become a respectable politician.

00:10:54.430 --> 00:10:57.480
After Season 2, Dawes’ actor left the show.

00:10:57.480 --> 00:11:03.949
But off-screen, Dawes continued to work, alongside
Fred Johnson, to make the OPA a legitimate

00:11:03.949 --> 00:11:06.949
Belter government, in peace with Earth and
Mars.

00:11:06.949 --> 00:11:10.319
The Earth government called him a “friend”.

00:11:10.319 --> 00:11:15.370
But some Belter extremists hated Dawes for
collaborating with the enemy – they called

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:19.080
him welwala, a traitor to his people.

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:24.190
And now Marco has risen up on a wave of violent
extremism.

00:11:24.190 --> 00:11:30.459
Last season he killed Fred Johnson, and now
he reveals he’s killed Dawes too.

00:11:30.459 --> 00:11:36.550
Marco has wiped out the moderate centre of
the OPA, and made himself the only option

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:38.131
for leadership of the Belt.

00:11:38.131 --> 00:11:39.131
In the books, Marco doesn’t kill Dawes.

00:11:39.131 --> 00:11:40.131
Dawes joins Marco.

00:11:40.131 --> 00:11:41.131
Dawes doesn’t like or trust Marco, but he
thinks that working with him and trying to

00:11:41.131 --> 00:11:42.131
guide Marco will be best for the Belt in the
long run.

00:11:42.131 --> 00:11:43.131
Though he pretty quickly realises that won’t
work.

00:11:43.131 --> 00:11:44.131
Marco installs Sanjrani as administrator of
Ceres.

00:11:44.131 --> 00:11:46.900
Sanjrani is a man in the books, but is non-binary
in the show.

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:50.350
And they’re trying to make a plan to grow
food for the Belt.

00:11:50.350 --> 00:11:54.879
Cause most of humanity’s food came from
Earth – so by attacking the planet, Marco

00:11:54.879 --> 00:11:59.870
has put billions at risk of starvation, including
the Belt.

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:04.399
Belt stations like Ganymede make food, and
the Free Navy’s also been stealing food

00:12:04.399 --> 00:12:06.550
from the colony ships heading out to the Ring.

00:12:06.550 --> 00:12:08.269
But it’s not enough.

00:12:08.269 --> 00:12:14.009
Unless they can build a sustainable system
to feed the Belt fast, millions of Belters

00:12:14.009 --> 00:12:16.670
will starve, along with those on Earth.

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:17.670
Marco may’ve freed the Belt.

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:18.670
But freedom isn’t worth much if you’re
dead.

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:22.600
Marco is not very interested in feeding his
people, and doesn’t really listen to Sanjrani.

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:27.470
Marco’s more interested in his personal
vendettas, wanting to hunt down Drummer and

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:28.779
Naomi.

00:12:28.779 --> 00:12:32.670
Marco doesn’t really care about the Belt.

00:12:32.670 --> 00:12:36.769
He cares about his own selfish desires and
ego.

00:12:36.769 --> 00:12:42.459
Marco’s son Filip uses his status as the
great leader’s son to get sex.

00:12:42.459 --> 00:12:48.060
Filip has a lot of complicated frustrated
feelings about his place in the world, his

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:53.110
parents, his need for intimacy, his guilt,
so maybe this is an emotional outlet for him.

00:12:53.110 --> 00:12:55.380
Or maybe he just likes sex.

00:12:55.380 --> 00:13:01.839
Filip acts rude and entitled, and he uses
people, just like his dad does.

00:13:01.839 --> 00:13:05.769
Filip’s friend Yoan has a vest made of alligator
skin.

00:13:05.769 --> 00:13:11.490
To him, it’s a trophy of victory to wear
a luxury item from the defeated Earth.

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:15.360
He says now that Earth’s environment is
broken, soon there won’t be any more of

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:20.319
this stuff – industry will collapse, animals
will go extinct.

00:13:20.319 --> 00:13:24.589
This could be “the last leather vest out
of Earth”.

00:13:24.589 --> 00:13:30.199
To Belters like Yoan and Filip that might
not mean much, they barely know what an alligator

00:13:30.199 --> 00:13:31.199
is.

00:13:31.199 --> 00:13:37.800
But to Earthers like, us, the cultural and
ecological death of Earth is a tragedy.

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:42.750
The Belters and the inners fail to see each
other’s perspective, and that’s what leads

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:46.240
to dehumanisation and atrocity.

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:51.779
Marco gives a speech about how Ceres will
be the capital of a new Belter nation.

00:13:51.779 --> 00:13:56.990
This dream of a Belter nation was shared by
Naomi, Ashford, and Fred.

00:13:56.990 --> 00:14:01.550
It’s a worthy goal, and Marco says all the
right things.

00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:03.860
But Filip knows it’s bullshit.

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:08.110
Marco’s not really willing to do the work
of building a nation.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:12.480
He’s not really the heroic leader he pretends
to be.

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:18.420
Filip does feel loyal to Marco, but he’s
increasingly full of doubts.

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:22.670
Filip and Yoan hang out with a couple of girls,
and brag about their victories with the Free

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:23.670
Navy.

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:27.430
But then Yoan brings up Filip’s role in
the attack on Earth.

00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:30.560
Filip stole the stealth tech that coated the
rocks.

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:34.100
Filip killed the scientists who saw the rocks
coming.

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:38.060
Filip helped kill millions of people.

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:43.740
Last season, Naomi told Filip that one day
he will feel guilt for that atrocity, and

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:47.319
that he’ll realise that Marco has made him
a murderer.

00:14:47.319 --> 00:14:53.639
Naomi’s words have had an impact on Filip,
so he leaves and wrestles with his feelings.

00:14:53.639 --> 00:14:59.110
Rosenfeld tells Marco that Medina Station
is installing “Laconian pieces”.

00:14:59.110 --> 00:15:04.430
We know Marco and Laconia made a deal that
Marco can rule the Sol system, and Duarte

00:15:04.430 --> 00:15:06.040
can rule Laconia.

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:11.310
So now it looks like Laconia is also providing
some.. technological support for Medina.

00:15:11.310 --> 00:15:14.990
Rosenfeld says they “need to reinforce the
abutments”.

00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:18.699
So.. what are they building in there?

00:15:18.699 --> 00:15:23.899
Filip tries to get involved, and says the
Free Navy must feed the Belt, but Marco and

00:15:23.899 --> 00:15:26.000
Rosenfeld brush him off.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:32.089
So again Filip is rejected by his father,
and feels he can’t help the Belt, so why

00:15:32.089 --> 00:15:33.089
is he here?

00:15:33.089 --> 00:15:35.190
What was all the fighting for?

00:15:35.190 --> 00:15:36.970
Was Naomi right?

00:15:36.970 --> 00:15:41.540
Filip doesn’t know how to handle all his
feelings, so he gets drunk and harasses a

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:42.860
bartender.

00:15:42.860 --> 00:15:48.329
When Yoan turns up, Filip starts a fight with
him, and then shoots him dead in a stupid

00:15:48.329 --> 00:15:51.250
drunk impulsive murder.

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:54.290
Filip has killed lots of people before.

00:15:54.290 --> 00:15:59.370
But Yoan was his friend, killed at his hands.

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:03.009
Will Filip finally face the consequences of
his violence?

00:16:03.009 --> 00:16:05.490
And how will Marco react?

00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:10.699
In the book, Filip just shoots a security
guy at a club, and the guy doesn’t die.

00:16:10.699 --> 00:16:16.920
So the show makes it much more dramatic by
having Filip kill a friend instead.

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:23.189
Drummer and her family are hunted by Marco’s
forces, after her betrayal of Marco last season.

00:16:23.189 --> 00:16:29.129
She lures an enemy ship into a trap with her
ship the DeWalt, which she controls remotely

00:16:29.129 --> 00:16:31.390
from her other ship the Tynan.

00:16:31.390 --> 00:16:35.579
But Drummer’s partner Michio fucks up and
presses the wrong button, forcing Drummer

00:16:35.579 --> 00:16:39.000
to blow up the DeWalt to destroy the enemy
ship.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:45.430
So Drummer loses a ship, and all the supplies
on it, because of Michio’s mistake.

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:49.490
Michio is one of Drummer’s partners in her
polyamorous family.

00:16:49.490 --> 00:16:53.620
But Michio isn’t a fighter, she isn’t
trained for war.

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:58.410
So Drummer decides to remove her from the
crew and leave her behind somewhere safe.

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:03.999
Last season, Drummer’s partner Serge was
killed, her partners Oksana and Bertold left.

00:17:03.999 --> 00:17:06.390
Now Michio’s gone too.

00:17:06.390 --> 00:17:24.000
How much more can Drummer lose to this war?

00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:28.020
Season 6 of the Expanse is the result of five
seasons of buildup.

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:33.840
A century of tension and resentment and between
Earth and the Belt is coming to a climactic

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:36.070
resolution.

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:39.669
And everyone’s relationships are being pushed
to breaking point.

00:17:39.669 --> 00:17:45.020
Can the families of the Roci crew, Drummer,
and Filip survive this conflict?

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:49.890
Can the inner planets and the Belt co-exist
without destroying each other?

00:17:49.890 --> 00:17:53.740
And, most importantly, what’s up with the
weird space dogs?

00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:56.600
There are five more episodes left of The Expanse.

00:17:56.600 --> 00:18:01.350
We’ll release a video all about the finale
of The Expanse on the day the last episode

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:02.409
comes out.

00:18:02.409 --> 00:18:05.570
Please subscribe to this channel, and give
it a comment and like.

00:18:05.570 --> 00:18:10.779
Thank you to Amazon Prime Video UK for sponsoring
and making these videos possible.

00:18:10.779 --> 00:18:11.389
Cheers.

